# Vite reads .env.production during `npm run build`, and the build runs *inside* the
# image. A developer's local `.env.production` (git-ignored, so it differs per machine)
# would otherwise be copied into the build context and decide what a released image
# points at. Build-args are the only supported input; the example file is documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
